        "bodyContent": "<h2 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>ATI TEAS Math Section at a Glance</strong></h2><p>The ATI TEAS Math section has 38 questions and a 57-minute time limit. It includes two scored sub-content areas: Numbers and Algebra, and Measurement and Data.</p><table style=\"min-width: 50px\"><colgroup><col style=\"min-width: 25px\"><col style=\"min-width: 25px\"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><strong>Detail</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><strong>Value</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>Total questions</p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>38</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>Scored questions</p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>34</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>Unscored questions</p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>4</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>Time limit</p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>57 minutes</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>Numbers and Algebra</p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>18 scored questions</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>Measurement and Data</p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p>16 scored questions</p></td></tr></tbody></table><div data-type=\"dotted-separator\" class=\"dotted-separator\"></div><p>A balanced practice plan should cover both calculation fluency and real problem setup. The calculator can help with arithmetic, but it cannot choose the equation for you.</p><div data-type=\"dotted-separator\" class=\"dotted-separator\"></div><h2 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>What Is the NursingMocks ATI TEAS Math Practice Test?</strong></h2><p>The NursingMocks ATI TEAS Math practice test is a helpful tool for students getting ready to take the nursing entrance exam, especially when it comes to the Math part. This practice test is not the actual ATI TEAS exam, but rather a way to prepare for it. It also does not take the place of the real test that you will schedule through ATI or your school.</p><p>You can use it to work on whole-number and rational-number operations, algebra setup, measurement, unit conversions, geometric quantities, data interpretation, and word problems. When you get a Math question wrong, it is not always because you do not know the math. Sometimes the mistake happens before you even start doing the math. You need to get the setup right before you can solve the problem.</p><h2 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>What Topics Are Covered?</strong></h2><p>The ATI TEAS Math section includes two official sub-content areas: Numbers and Algebra, and Measurement and Data. NursingMocks helps you practice Math by focusing on these same areas, so you can see which types of problems you need to work on.</p><h3 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>Numbers and Algebra Practice Questions</strong></h3><p>Numbers and Algebra practice focuses on whole-number and rational-number operations, fractions, decimals, percentages, ratios, proportions, expressions, equations, and word problems. Many misses come from setting up the wrong relationship, not from the final arithmetic.</p><h3 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>Measurement and Data Practice Questions</strong></h3><p>Measurement and Data practice focuses on unit conversions, area, perimeter, volume, geometric quantities, charts, graphs, tables, data comparison, and interpretation. Units are a clue. If the answer asks for square units, volume, rate, or percentage, the unit often tells you what kind of setup is needed.</p><h2 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>ATI TEAS Math Question Presentation and Problem Styles</strong></h2><p>The way questions are asked can be different in each NursingMocks <u>Math set</u>, but what really matters is what kind of math problem you are trying to solve.</p><p>When you are faced with a Math problem, you might need to solve an equation, turn a word problem into numbers, compare quantities, understand what a table is telling you, read a chart, or pick the right unit to use. Before you start doing any math, take a moment to think about what the question is actually asking for.</p><h2 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>How Math Practice Works on NursingMocks</strong></h2><p>To begin, pick a <u>Math set</u> from the ATI TEAS practice area. Read the question slowly, figure out what it is asking for, set up the problem, and then do the math. After you choose an answer, check whether it is right and compare it to how you set up the problem. This helps you understand where you might have gone wrong.</p><p>When an explanation is provided, look for the first place your work split from the correct method. That is usually more useful than only checking the final number.</p><p>Use each completed set to decide what to practice next. Repeated missed patterns matter more than one bad question.</p><h2 class=\"custom-heading\"><strong>Timed ATI TEAS Math Practice</strong></h2><p>The Math section gives you 57 minutes to answer 38 questions, which averages about 90 seconds for each one. Some questions are quick and just need a simple calculation, but word problems, conversions, and data questions can take longer.</p><p>Math pacing usually breaks down in the setup. If you rush the setup, the calculator can give you a precise answer to the wrong problem. Estimate when it helps you catch an unreasonable result.</p><p>After a timed set, check where time went: rereading the question, choosing the operation, converting units, or recalculating because the first answer looked wrong.</p><h2 class=\"custom-heading\">Review Your Math Answers, Explanations, and Results</h2><p>When you are done with a <u>Math set</u>, take a closer look at the questions that gave you trouble, the ones you had to guess at, or the ones that took you a while to answer. Usually, the Math questions you miss can be grouped into a few main categories.</p><ul><li><p>Setup error: You chose the wrong operation, equation, proportion, or relationship.</p></li><li><p>Calculation error: The setup was right, but the arithmetic or calculator entry was wrong.</p></li><li><p>Unit error: You missed a conversion, label, rate, area, volume, or percentage relationship.</p></li><li><p>Question-reading error: You solved for something different from what the question asked.</p></li></ul><p>Do not treat all wrong answers the same. If the setup was wrong, doing more arithmetic drills will not fix the real problem. Use the most common error type to choose your next <u>Math set</u> or <u>topic review</u>.</p><section data-eyebrow=\"\" data-title=\"Start ATI TEAS Math Practice\" data-description=\"Choose a NursingMocks Math set and begin practicing calculations, word problems, conversions, measurement, and data interpretation. After each set, review missed questions and use the patterns you notice to plan your next practice activity.\" data-button-label=\"ATI TEAS Practice Test \" data-button-href=\"/teas-7-practice-test\" data-type=\"cta-block\" class=\"public-cta-block\"><div class=\"public-cta-block-copy\"><div class=\"public-cta-block-eyebrow\">Ready to practice?</div><h3>Start your practice session</h3><p>Choose a subject, answer exam-style questions, and review explanations.</p></div><a class=\"public-cta-block-button\" href=\"#\">Start Practice</a></section><p></p>",
